#: .\templates\Lobby\fcmNewCode.html:19
msgid "New FCM code"
msgstr ""

#: .\templates\Lobby\fcmNewCode.html:21
msgid "What's this about?"
msgstr ""

#: .\templates\Lobby\fcmNewCode.html:23
msgid ""
"In short, FCM needed a big recode. It is mainly under-the-hood things, so "
"you hopefully won't notice that much difference. <br /> That being said, "
"there are a lot of internal changes, so keep an eye an things, and report "
"any new bugs that you find."
msgstr ""

#: .\templates\Lobby\fcmNewCode.html:30
msgid "What isn't 'Under-the-hood'?"
msgstr ""

#: .\templates\Lobby\fcmNewCode.html:32
msgid ""
"I've added the ability to play the whole payday / fridge phase after your "
"working day turn. <br /> So instead of simply paying for everyone / no-one, "
"you can pre-fire employees as you wish. <br /> You can also pre-set which "
"items you'd like to store in your fridge, in priority order. <br /> <br /> "
"There is also a summary at the end of the working day to show what you did "
"in each sub-phase, and remind you if you missed anything. <br /> <br /> For "
"restructuring, you now have a mini-beach visible at all times, and can "
"directly select cards from there."
msgstr ""

#: .\templates\Lobby\fcmNewCode.html:47
msgid "Why did it need a rewrite?"
msgstr ""

#: .\templates\Lobby\fcmNewCode.html:49
#, python-format
msgid ""
"99%% of the time it didn't. But very occasionally it would do odd things. "
"<br /> EG after the first turn of a game that had salaried employees that it "
"was possible to directly hire, the game would pause until every player had "
"\"looked\" at the game, before moving on automatically if they didn't need "
"to pay anything. <br /> Sometimes it would display oddly if you had the MS "
"to pay in food.<br/> Occasionally it would wait during the marketing phase "
"until a certain player had looked at the game. <br/> <br/> These should be "
"fixed, as well as making it easier to fix and improve the code in the future."
msgstr ""

#: .\templates\Lobby\fcmNewCode.html:62
msgid "Was it worth it?"
msgstr ""

#: .\templates\Lobby\fcmNewCode.html:64
#, python-format
msgid ""
"Ha, well it took literally 10s of hours to do; probably over 100 i guess, "
"with the improvements added as well.<br/> But it was needed to fix those 1%% "
"situations, and make the code a lot easier to work with in the future!"
msgstr ""

