#: .\templates\Lobby\tournamentsHelp.html:21
msgid "When are the tournaments?"
msgstr ""

#: .\templates\Lobby\tournamentsHelp.html:25
msgid ""
"<b>Indonesia, Horseless Carriage, Antiquity, and Bus</b>: Tournaments are "
"run at regular intervals<br/> They open on 1st of the month, and start on "
"7th, or later if more people are needed. <br/> The format is randomly chosen "
"from Rounds, Two Lives, and Points."
msgstr ""

#: .\templates\Lobby\tournamentsHelp.html:35
msgid "Month"
msgstr ""

#: .\templates\Lobby\tournamentsHelp.html:60
msgid "What are the formats?"
msgstr ""

#: .\templates\Lobby\tournamentsHelp.html:62
msgid ""
"<b>Rounds</b> consists of (currently) 4 rounds, where all players are "
"included in the games, after which there is a short knockout of all players "
"on top points to determine the overall winner. <br /> <br /> <b>Two Lives</"
"b> is like double elimination; once you've lose twice then you're out of the "
"tournament. <br /> <br /> <b>Points</b> functions the same as Rounds, except "
"that instead of “winner takes all”, points awards points per position - "
"unlike the other formats which are winner takes all. 5 player games award "
"16 / 8 / 4 / 2 / 1 points, 4 player games award 8 / 4 / 2 / 1 points, and 3 "
"player games award 4 / 2 / 1 points per position (note that in a single "
"tournaments all games will have the same number of players). <br /> <br /> "
"<b>Knockout</b> is simply the winner moves to the next round. This format "
"will not be used in the regular schedule above, in order to get all players "
"more games."
msgstr ""

#: .\templates\Lobby\tournamentsHelp.html:81
msgid "How are game players decided?"
msgstr ""

#: .\templates\Lobby\tournamentsHelp.html:83
msgid ""
"Initially game players are drawn randomly. After this, players are ranked by "
"number of wins / (or points in a points. tournament). In 2p, players will "
"play the closest people to them that thay haven't already played. For 3p+ "
"the system will try to group people who haven’t played together, but there’s "
"a higher chance you might end up seeing the same person more than once. <br /"
"> If there are any players left over, they receive a \"Bye\", which counts "
"as an automatic win (or half max points in a points tournament), and "
"progress to the next round. \"Byes\" will generally be given to the lowest "
"ranked players, and are limited to one per tournament. Essentially \"Byes\" "
"are given randomly to the lowest ranked player who hasn't yet had a \"Bye\"."
msgstr ""

#: .\templates\Lobby\tournamentsHelp.html:98
msgid ""
"If someone is kicked out then they are ejected from the tournament. They "
"will lose both lives in Two Lives, and be removed from a Rounds/Points "
"tournament."
msgstr ""

#: .\templates\Lobby\tournamentsHelp.html:104
msgid "What else should I know?"
msgstr ""

#: .\templates\Lobby\tournamentsHelp.html:106
msgid ""
"Players will not play the same person again until there's no other option "
"(currently applies to 2p games, and the first 2 players in larger "
"playercounts). <br /> Players will not receive two \"byes\" until there's no "
"other option. <br /> Kickout timer will be 1 day, with the exception of the "
"first move which will be 3 days, in case players don't realise a game has "
"started. <br /> Notifications are sent out at the start of every new "
"tournament game. If you finish quickly there could be several days until "
"your next game starts, so it is strongly recommended to have at least one "
"form of notification enabled in your profile."
msgstr ""

